//
// vllm-sr/d3-edge (BF16, default weight form) decision latency vs prompt length, into
// d3_edge.prefill_sweep.json (collected by the nightly LLM benchmark). d3 has no
// decode: the latency of one System One question, from the token ids to the
// option probabilities, is its time to first token. One prefill device serves
// every length; each length is timed in one process on a single question of
// exactly that many tokens (make profile-fused-prefill).
//
// Latency only, never a correctness gate (run_npu2_verify.lit is that).
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, peano_ge22, hf_token, hfweights_vllm_sr_d3_edge
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: cd test_peano_prefill_sweep
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% %PYTHON %S/../bench/sweep_prefill.py --model-name d3_edge --makefile %S/Makefile --lengths 512,1024,2048,4096 --fused --peano-dir %PEANO_INSTALL_DIR --out d3_edge.prefill_sweep.json
// RUN: FileCheck %s < d3_edge.prefill_sweep.json
// CHECK: "model": "d3_edge"
// CHECK: "axis": "prefill_len"
// CHECK: "prefill_len": 2048
// CHECK-NEXT: "ttft_ms": {{[0-9]}}
